Z||000002||82-T/A||12-06-2000||09:24 AM||||Hey, thats pretty cool! Much respect to you.<P>I too have an Iron Duke Fiero.<P>While I also have a V6 87, my main priority first is to fix up my 84.<P>I'll post some pictures when I've got them too, but the paint is original and immaculate. IMHO, it's the best looking body style. Mine is red too.<P>I am also keeping the motor when I give it a good once over.<P>My plan is to rebuild it with the performance rebuild kit from the Fiero Store.<P>That includes forged pistons, new bearings, Hi-Flow oil pump, Hooker Header, Sealed Power camshaft, shift kit, and a K&N air filter. <P>With the exception of the hooker header (still not TOTALLY decided on that yet) the car will otherwise look COMPLETELY stock. Which is the look I prefer. Only other mod I've done.. which of course is more for aesthetics, is I replaced the stock exhaust tip with the chrome plated tips from the Ocelot exhaust. I bought that for my V6, kept the stock tips on my V6, and took the left hand side tip from the Ocelot and put it on my 84. It looks factory.<P>Anyway, nice car... what kind of times do you run? <P>I am hoping to run high 15s with these mods.<P>I figure with those mods, it should get me into the high 15s.. about like a Fiero V6. <P>If it's still not quick enough, I can have brass valve guides installed and higher ratio roller rockers.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
